so last time on true fear I talked about  the LA sleepwalker  if you haven't seen that video click  here and you can go check it out so I  never saw the El a sleepwalker again but  I did make a habit of going out there to  check to see if it was a habit that he  was doing it every night or something he  wasn't but what I did notice is some  other very strange things around my  apartment complex now this was not a  nice apartment by any standards but it  was student housing and it was close to  school I wish I had never stayed there  but there's nothing I do about it now so  anyways there's all these closets  scattered around the apartment complex  and usually they're just closed and  locked  but when I got back one night from going  to check for the sleepwalker I noticed  that one of them was open and none of  them have ever been opened before so me  and my roommates go to investigate and  we just find all of this crazy stuff  inside of the closet lawn chairs cones a  shovel just all of these random objects  that anyone who lives in an apartment  would never really need I don't remember  all of the exact items though and the  thing that was really weird about this  is that none of our resident keys gave  access to any of the closets so if these  closets weren't for residents storage  then who were they for so we decided to  do a little investigating and check out  all the doors in the apartment complex  that didn't lead to other people's units  most of the closets were either locked  or empty but we did discover two new  doors that we could access one was at  the end of our hallway which you can  actually see here in dead air and the  other one was on the hallway opposite of  ours and they both led to these secret  stairways which probably weren't a  secret to the stoners of that apartment  building because they both smelled like  weed the stairway closest to us had a  doorway leading out to the side alley  well the one on the other side did not  we always thought that the main  staircase which you can see right here  in acrimonious was the only way to get  up or down in the building because  whatever labels that had been on these  stairwells to tell you that they were  stairs had been torn off but the most  important part was at the top of each  stair well there were two doors one  leading back to the resident hallways  and one leading to we don't know what so  we wanted to figure out what these other  doors led to at the top of the staircase  closest to us the door was locked but on  the other side it was open  behind the door there's this tiny closet  and in the back of the closet there's  this metal hatch about two feet by two  feet so we open the hatch and it leads  to the chute we look down in the chute  and there's the secret room underneath  and we had no idea how to access this  room from the rest of the building and  we had no idea that it existed before so  I poked my head down there and it was  pitch black but with the help of a phone  light we were able to see a few things  there were some boxes some canned food  and a sleeping bag so I immediately  pulled my light out of there because  what's going through my head is there's  someone living down there and if they  see the light they're probably gonna  walk underneath and look back at us and  if something like that did happen I  imagine the person would probably be  enraged that we found out that they were  living down there because let's face it  the management at that building  however lazy they may be probably  wouldn't be too happy if there was  someone secretly living inside and they  would be likely to investigate actually  on second thought that management  literally didn't care about us at all  but that would be considered trespassing  if somebody was down there so if  somebody found out they could  potentially get the police involved  think about if you were living down  there and somebody found out about you  that's potentially threatening like your  entire existence your entire way of  living you would probably want to do  something about it and I know that  sounds kind of overdramatic but you have  to keep in mind that these people on the  streets in LA are there for a reason  it's a sad reality but you see a lot of  people who are mentally ill or at least  like mentally unstable so honestly the  idea of somebody seeing us and coming  after us was not entirely out of the  question  especially considering the fact that we  have nowhere to hide because they know  that we live in those apartments and  they could easily follow us back or lurk  by the entrance until we go in or out  and I know this whole thing might sound  a little over-the-top considering we had  no actual evidence that anyone was  living down there just a top-down view  of some canned food in a sleeping bag  but you have to remember that I have a  very dark imagination and there was  enough evidence to at least confirm that  there was something going on so we went  back to our apartment and started  discussing what we had seen and thus the  idea of the hobo king was born or at  least it started as just an idea  being creative people we came up with  this whole scenario in character  revolving around the hobo king in our  story  the hobo king is actually a very smart  man who figured out how to live his life  safely and efficiently without needing  to get a job and has since reached out  to other homeless people in the area to  help give them a shelter overnight  so he dubbed himself that hobo King and  started donning tattered robes made up  of rags and one of those Burger King  birthday crowns that he found in the  dumpster  he's a very egotistical character so  over time he amassed all these followers  and he gave them a place to stay in  exchange for collecting taxes from the  people off the streets so if you're  homeless and you want to stay in the  hobo king's castle if you will you could  do so by giving him 20% of the earnings  that you made begging by the freeway  ramp so that's the extent of what we  made up the rest of this is all real  I'll still be referring to the homeless  person as the hobo king for the rest of  the story then so from that point  forward we started checking up in the  closets and monitoring what was going on  in the property after the staff left  every night and what we found was that  while all the closets are usually locked  every now and then a random one of them  would be left open and we would just  find more weird things inside with that  one door at the end of the staircase  that led to the chute was always open we  think that somebody left it open a while  ago one of the staff members and perhaps  forgot about it and it's just been left  open ever since but the question still  remained how was the hobo king getting  access to this supposedly gated property  who is the one getting inside and  granting access to all of these doors  and closets to answer that we looked at  the three types of people who have  access to the property the residents the  managers and the maintenance guy anyone  else who came onto the property like  pest control for example was an  independent worker and didn't have  access to anything as I mentioned  earlier as residents we didn't have  access to any of those doors because  none of our keys worked on them so that  just left the manager and the  maintenance guy both of them were  absolutely awful the manager would  really only stop in for about an hour  every day to meet with potential leases  and then leave right after that we know  this because whenever we had a problem  and we tried to get ahold of the manager  it was impossible and we would end up  just having to wait around all day by  the managers office that just leaves us  with the maintenance guy who was  abhorrent ly lazy whenever we had an  issue he would just show up like a week  later with one of his friends yes he  would just bring some of his friends to  work with him sometime  we would tell him about the problem we  were having he would be like oh ok I'll  be right back and then he would leave  and never come back  but we did notice that he would spend a  lot of time behind closed doors in his  office talking to one of his friends  that he had brought to work which led me  to this theory one of the maintenance  guys friends is the hobo King the  maintenance guy feels bad for him and  leaves him open a closet or room to stay  in each night after the hobo King gains  some followers he convinces the  maintenance guy to let a few of them  stay as well over time it leads to an  infestation this theory is backed up  because during the day when the  maintenance guy was in is when all the  locks would get changed  which was also when we were away at  class we would also see the maintenance  guy roaming around with a huge keyring  with dozens and dozens of keys and  finally the maintenance guy was always  in his office but he was never actually  out maintaining or fixing anything  we continued to keep tabs and all the  activity that was taking place around  the apartment complex but what we really  wanted to know is how to access that  secret room with the exception of  opening the hatch and thrown a rope and  climbing down and then being stuck down  there with a potentially crazy homeless  person and no exit we assumed that the  chute and another chute that we assumed  also exists on the stairwell by our side  we're both garbage chutes at one time  that they just got too lazy to keep  taking to the street and then move the  dumpsters to the street for us to take  our garbage out to if that's true then  there had to be an entrance somewhere  most likely and the two alleyways on  either side of the building first we  checked the alleyway on our side we  didn't find a secret door on our side  but we did find like this all these  scuba books and scuba equipment that had  just been scattered out in the alley for  some reason I really don't know what to  make of that that doesn't even have to  do with the story at all but I just  thought I'd throw that in there we had  to hop a fence to access the alleyway on  the other side a fence that seemed to be  guarding nothing but an empty alleyway  until we found a door on the side of the  building that lined up with the exact  location where the secret room should be  we were actually pretty nervous to go  inside because what if there was a  homeless person living in there right  now  but we wanted answers so we decided to  just quietly go inside and see if there  was anything going on in there so I go  down the alleyway to open the door  my roommates get ready to run if need be  I turn the handle and the door's locked  but here's the thing we don't know if  it's locked from the inside or the  outside so just to play it safe we book  it all the way back to the other side  all the way back until we're safe inside  of our apartment so for a while we're  just sitting there discussing it and  kind of building on the lore of the hobo  king so in the apartment we have this  big rear projection TV and while we were  talking I kept looking over at the  window because I felt like I saw  something moving and I should add that  the window leads to the alleyway on our  side and then at one point I thought I  saw something on the TV but the TV was  off this was a reflection and in the  reflection I see the outline of a man's  head and staring through the window I  look over to the window and the man's  gone I look back to the TV to see if it  was maybe something else and whatever it  was was gone  all I can see in the reflection is the  empty window now I'm not gonna  immediately cry hobo King because we did  make that character up but I don't think  it's out of the question to suggest that  there may have been someone living in  the building or maybe not I mean we had  a neighbor who lived next to us who had  somebody break in through his window so  it really could have been anybody but  there is one more chapter to this story  we didn't end up staying at the  apartment complex much longer than that  and no we did not leave because of the  hobo King but basically what happened is  there is this leak in our ceiling and  the maintenance guy was too lazy to fix  it and it turned into a hole in the  ceiling and once the hole formed in the  ceiling we got bedbugs and it was just  this whole huge disaster the bedbugs  were a fate far worse than any hobo King  are really far worse than anything at  all it was an awful experience but  that's a whole nother story but anyways  we were kind of getting over the whole  hobo king thing because we hadn't seen  anything in a while but before we left  we were walking around and we noticed  that there was one more closet door that  had been left open and it wasn't one  that we had previously seen open at any  time before so we opened it there was  some electrical panels wires and  switches  plant but on the floor there was a  blanket and pillow and it wasn't like  they were folded up and stored in the  corner they were laid out like an actual  bed but the craziest part of any of this  was in the closet  there was a bunch of graffiti on the  walls and they were mostly just like  so-and-so was here and pictures of  penises and what-have-you  but there is this one little bit of text  that completely blew my mind  it said King so as we were filming this  my buddy West Dakota who is helping me  film these videos actually mentioned  that he has a little bit more  information that I wasn't even aware of  so I'm gonna hand it over to him so this  apartment complex ended the contract  with our school due to a whole slew of  issues but a couple months before that  contract ended hanging up around the  complex were signs telling the residents  to make sure that the gates were closed  because there were a bunch of homeless  people getting into the complex and  sleeping in the closets you've been told  about so that just confirms the story a  little bit more about how there were  homeless people staying in this  apartment complex and I didn't even know  that going into this I just asked Dakota  to come to help me make a video he  didn't know that I was recording this at  all and he just happened to stumble upon  that little bit of information this was  the last of what I have to tell about  the hobo King I was actually working on  a found footage webseries for a while  based on our apartment complex and our  idea of what the hobo King might be it  included characters that represented  each of us as well as some new made-up  characters sadly I never got to shoot it  before the bed bugs forced us out of  that place and the script really did  rely on the geographical layout of that  complex however after the bed bugs we  found ourselves hopping around from  hotel to hotel for a while so on the  next episode of true fear I'll be  telling you guys about the crazy woman  in one of the rooms leave your own  theories about the hobo king in the  comments if we get 200 likes on this  video I will read you guys the script  for my found-footage web series about  the hobo king either here or on my other  series all dainty creepypasta so make  sure to share this video get it out  there get it some likes and as always  don't forget to subscribe and I will see  you in the next video  assuming we both  five
 

